City Builder assets and where they come from.

Every asset shipped with the mod is listed here with its source, author, licence and whether it was changed. Assets
whose source or licence is unknown are not added.

Made for this mod (no outside sources), under the mod's licence (MIT, see LICENSE):

Textures (textures/block/), each drawn by a script in tools/textures/:

  road_textures.py
    asphalt.png, asphalt_white.png, asphalt_hatch.png, road_arrow_shaft.png, road_arrow_head.png, manhole.png,
    drain_grate.png, tactile_line.png, tactile_dot.png, sidewalk.png, sidewalk_side.png (the kerb),
    sidewalk_interlocking.png, sidewalk_granite.png, curb.png, and line/<colour>_<angle>_<offset>.png (the road
    markings, white and yellow, at 16 angles and 8 offsets)

  landmark_textures.py
    track.png, turf.png, turf_dark.png, turf_side.png, soil.png, seat_<colour>.png, fresnel_lens.png, led_panel.png,
    and line/{track,turf,turf_dark,soil}_white_*.png. The stadium seat's steel bracket uses the game's own light grey
    concrete texture by reference (nothing copied).

  temple_blocks.py
    ishidatami.png, shirasu.png, tamajari.png, koke*.png, raked_gravel*.png, tobiishi_stone.png, niwaishi.png,
    bamboo_fence*.png, tatami*.png, fusuma*.png, shoji*.png, ranma*.png, coffered_ceiling*.png, zabuton.png, koro*.png,
    chochin*.png, shimenawa.png, shide.png, saisen_bako*.png. The moss block's bottom refers to the game's own dirt
    texture (nothing copied).

  airport_textures.py
    curtain_wall_*.png, metal_roof*.png, ceiling_light.png, terminal_tile.png, carpet_tile_*.png, seat_fabric.png,
    seat_frame.png, sign/*.png, flight_board.png, panel_side.png, bridge_bellows.png and bridge_cladding.png (the
    boarding bridges), baggage_belt*.png, escalator_*.png. The pictograms are drawn there in the manner of airport
    signs, not copied from any standard's artwork.

  bridge_textures.py
    concrete_parapet*.png, bridge_railing*.png, bridge_bearing*.png, sound_barrier*.png, steel_girder_*.png,
    expansion_joint.png, deck_side.png, deck_drain.png, drain_pipe.png

  catenary_textures.py
    catenary_*.png, curve_marker_*.png

  sign_textures.py
    sign/blade_*.png, sign/fascia_*.png (shops' projecting signs, fascia boards and lit fascias). Their lettering is
    strokes put together by the script, no script's characters and no brand's.

Block states, block and item models (blockstates/, models/), loot tables (data/citybuilder/loot_tables/) and the
translations (lang/): written for this mod, by the *_models.py scripts in tools/textures/ or by hand.

Not shipped: the building library's structure templates are generated from parameters (core.building) or from
PLATEAU's city models (tools/assets/plateau_voxel.py) into the build folder; any of them shipped later is listed here
with its source and the credit its licence asks for.

Data used for statistics only (nothing of it is shipped):

PLATEAU (Japan's Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism, and the cities; the cities' site policies,
compatible with CC BY 4.0): building footprints, heights and uses of Kyoto, Kanazawa, Himeji, Tokyo's Taito and Chuo,
measured by tools/assets/plateau_*.py for the lots' sizes, the streets' uses, the blocks' insides and the buildings'
sizes.

OpenStreetMap (OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0): streets and buildings of Kyoto, Kanazawa, Takayama,
Hida-Furukawa, Shimoda, Karuizawa, Nikko, Himeji and Tokyo, measured by the cityMap and osmStats tools and
tools/assets/osm_buildings.py for the street network's and the buildings' targets.
